cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Faithful formalization: Milnor's Topology from the Differentiable Viewpoint and Morse Theory in Lean 4"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Yongzhong
    affiliation: Kinglake Research LLC
repository-code: "https://github.com/skydancerosel/math_faithful"
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/skydancerosel/math_faithful/blob/main/LICENSE"
date-released: 2026-10-23
version: "1.0"
abstract: >-
  Complete formalizations against Mathlib of John Milnor's Topology from the Differentiable
  Viewpoint and Morse Theory, with a human-readable layer that shows, statement by statement,
  how the formal results relate to the book's: a verified edition with a sign-off list, the
  formal proofs retold as mathematics with a trace tag on every step, a comparison of each
  result of the book with the formal statement, and a round-trip audit in which the book's
  statements were formalized blind and compared with the project's in Lean. The Lean code is
  under the Apache License 2.0; the prose (expositions, reports) is under CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formalization
  - Morse theory
  - differential topology
  - Bott periodicity
